From: lagz0ne <15101444+lagz0ne@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 02:07:03 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 10/28] feat(review): a review role, a changes-requested
 verdict and its event

Human reviewers should look, comment and give a verdict, approve or send a
frame back, without being able to change the design. Until now giving a
verdict needed edit rights, and there was no way to say "not yet".

- Roles rank view < comment < review < edit (shared/canvasRole.ts). review
  is everything comment is, plus the verdict; every frame write, the room's
  editing messages and the drawing tools still need edit. It is not a link
  level, and nothing grants it yet beyond edit including it (the embedded
  review panel will).
- PUT /api/frames/:id/approval needs review and takes ready_for_dev,
  changes_requested or draft. changes_requested is the same record as an
  approval (who, when, which revision). setFrameApproval takes the verdict
  instead of a boolean and writes "requested changes on ..." to activity.
- A design edit after either verdict makes the frame needs_review, as it
  already did after an approval.
- The approval keeps `verdict`, the last verdict given, which the flip to
  needs_review does not erase, and `history`, the last 20 verdicts oldest
  first ({ status, by, byUserId, at, frameUpdatedAt, versionId }). A
  verdict files the state it was given on as a design version (savedAt =
  the frame's updatedAt then), because versions are kept per burst of edits
  and a tweak joining the open burst would never file it: the review panel
  compares against that versionId. persist's saveFrameVersion takes
  { always } so that snapshot is never skipped as a duplicate. Moving to
  draft clears the approval, history included; an approval from before
  history starts one from its own record (priorVerdicts).
- Editor: a frame revised after changes were requested says so ("Changes
  requested by X on D; revised since", en and pt-BR), not "previously
  approved".
- Each verdict emits a frame.approval canvas event: a webhook event of the
  same name ({ status, actor, frame }), listed in Settings (en, pt-BR).
- Agents: MCP get_canvas filters approval_status=changes_requested, and the
  MCP instructions, the guide and the resident agent's prompt say what it
  means (read the comments, revise; the edit asks for another review).
- Editor: the frame menu's verdict items (Mark ready for dev, and the new
  Request changes) need review, lock/delete still need edit; the Inspector
  has Request changes beside the approval switch; the badge reads "Changes
  requested" with who and when (en, pt-BR).

Tests: reviewVerdicts.test.ts (real server: a comment-link visitor is
refused, an editor sends a frame back, the webhook delivery, needs_review
after an edit, a new verdict on the new revision; verdict and history
through an edit, the reviewed state's version even when the next tweak
joins its burst, the cap of 20, draft clearing it), approvalHistory
(an approval from before history), frameApprovalControl
(Request changes, the badge, a reviewer's menu without editing items),
canvasRole (the ranking). approvalAutomations, frameApproval, webhooks,
webhookRoutes, mcp-tools, i18n, shareLinkRoles, guestCanvas, access pass.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
